mod:store_path_hops;
// 2026-11-13 (landing 177d2b6, row 1: DEF-644's K1). A STORE'S DESTINATION IS RESOLVED AT EACH POINTER-TYPED HOP OF ITS OWN PATH. `record_refs_through_indirection`
// resolved one indirection's targets: a store such as `(<-((<-sp).q)).lp = hq;` stopped at the first indirection's targets, or read the root's chain for the
// last one alone, so the stored pointer was recorded one hop short (on `s`, never on `m`). A pointer taken through the stored copy, then the `List` grown, then
// the pointer read, read freed heap. K1 lists the indirections on the destination's path, the last first (`path_indirections`), and walks them level by level
// (`rrti_path`): a target of an upper level that is a local of this frame is walked down by its own chain, and the last level's targets take the stored refs.
// One cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's. Each face is accepted by main (8a2b40b), by 169d6d4 and by b510126 (177d2b3), and reads freed memory there
// (236 at -O0 and -O2 on roads 0 to 2, 97 under the detector). Each right control is in `store_path_hops_ok.npk`. The row closes 30 faces. It refuses 14 right
// programs, each at parity with its by-name twin, named at the end of this comment.
// DEF-644's 26 (its register row's open faces, "OPEN, F on main and on the final (57)"; the attacks' cells on 177d2b4's final): `m1`, `m2`, `m3`, `m4`, `m1b`,
// `m7`, `m8`, `m9`, `s1b`, `arpp`, `arpp3`, `t_fldd`, and the grid's `sm` and `spp` columns (`call`, `q` and `ter`, each `a` and `b`): BORROW-015 at the growth.
// `kA1` and `kA1x` (DEF-633's road through a member, into a consuming `pick` arm's binding): BORROW-009 at the store, DEF-633's sentence.
// `pb`'s TWO (Ailp-team_109's cells; management_37's addendum 5 of Wed 11-11 23:53 EST: "Both go to row 4 as faces."): `SQN->:pb = @b; (<-((<-pb).q)).lp = hq;`,
// `xk_pb_L_F` over a local and `xk_pb_P_F` over a by-value parameter. BORROW-015 at the store's line.
// `fa_adr`'s TWO (nitpick-compiler_106's probes; management_38's ruling of Thu 11-12 01:19 EST: "is DEF-644's `pb` form (addendum 5). Row 5 measures it."; found
// on this row's whole cells, management_42's ruling of Fri 11-13 04:45:10 EST): `pb`'s store over a `for` binding,
// `for (SQN:b in sa) { SQN->:bp = @b; (<-((<-bp).q)).lp = hq; }` (`fa_adr`), and its local twin (`fa_adr_L`). BORROW-015 at the store's line.
// DEF-644's OPEN FACES BESIDE THESE, NOT CLOSED BY THIS ROW (F on every build, the row's `.ll` equal to main's): `xk_pbp_L_F`, `xk_pbp_P_F`, `xk_pbp_R_F` and
// `xk_pbp_RL_F` (Ailp-team_109's), `HPZ->->:pp = @((<-pb).q); (<-(<-pp)).lp = hq;`, a store through a pointer to a pointer whose target is reached through a pointer
// local (addendum 5: "If its candidate doesn't refuse it, it's DEF-644's open face beside `vd1`/`vd2`, and it goes to the next landing."). Not in this file.
// THE ROW'S PRICES: 14 RIGHT PROGRAMS, REFUSED, EACH AT PARITY WITH ITS BY-NAME TWIN. Each ran 67 on every road on main, 169d6d4 and b510126. Each twin spells the
// store by the binding's own name, and main refuses it with the same code (management_42's ruling of Fri 11-13 03:25:36 EST, item 1: "It refuses the same 14
// controls, each at parity with main's by-name twin."). Each fails closed.
// The grid's twelve `_l_ok`, the `sm` and `spp` columns' controls with the growth moved after the read, so the pointer is held to the end of its block:
// `g_sm_call_a_l_ok`, `g_sm_call_b_l_ok`, `g_sm_q_a_l_ok`, `g_sm_q_b_l_ok`, `g_sm_ter_a_l_ok`, `g_sm_ter_b_l_ok`, `g_spp_call_a_l_ok`, `g_spp_call_b_l_ok`,
// `g_spp_q_a_l_ok`, `g_spp_q_b_l_ok`, `g_spp_ter_a_l_ok`, `g_spp_ter_b_l_ok` (2026-11-13): BORROW-015 at the growth (the `ter` ones twice), as main refuses each
// one's by-name twin `g_nm_<call|q|ter>_<a|b>_l_ok` (`m.lp = hq;`) at the same codes and the same sites; each twin's `_n_ok` runs 67.
// `m9c_ok` (2026-11-13): BORROW-015 at its store, the same sentence as main's refusal of its by-name twin `m9n_ok`; `m9d_ok`, which declares `e` at the read, runs 67.
// `kA1xc_ok` (2026-11-13): BORROW-009 at its store, DEF-633's sentence, as main refuses its by-name twin `kA1xn_ok` (`m.lp = hq;` in the arm).
error:E5;
struct:K_m1 = { int64:k; };
struct:H_m1 = { List<int64>:l; int64:k; K_m1:kk; };
func:mk_m1 = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(1i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); pass l; };
func:mkh_m1 = H_m1() never fails { pass H_m1{ l: raw mk_m1(), k: 2i64, kk: K_m1{ k: 3i64 } }; };
func:growh_m1 = int64(H_m1->:w) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(@w.l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:growl_m1 = int64(List<int64>->:l) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:fp_m1 = int64->(H_m1->:q) never fails { pass @((<-q).l[0i64]); };
func:idh_m1 = H_m1->(H_m1->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:getl_m1 = List<int64>->(H_m1->:w) never fails { pass @w.l; };
struct:HPO_m1 = { H_m1->:lp; List<int64>:own; };
struct:SQ_m1 = { HPO_m1->:q; int64:z; };
struct:SR_m1 = { SQ_m1->:sq; int64:z; };
func:g_m1 = int64(H_m1->:h0p, H_m1->:hq, H_m1->:hz, int64:n) never fails {
    int64->:e = raw fp_m1(hz);
    HPO_m1:m = HPO_m1{ lp: h0p, own: raw mk_m1() }; SQ_m1:s = SQ_m1{ q: @m, z: 1i64 }; SQ_m1->:sp = @s;
    (<-((<-sp).q)).lp = hq;
    e = raw fp_m1(m.lp);
    discard(raw growh_m1(hq));
    pass (<-e) + 6i64;
};
func:f_m1 = int64(int64:n) never fails {
    H_m1:hz = raw mkh_m1(); H_m1:h0 = raw mkh_m1(); H_m1:h2 = raw mkh_m1();
    pass raw g_m1(@h0, @h2, @hz, n);
};
func:cell_main_m1 = int32() never fails { pass (((raw f_m1(1i64)) + 60i64) =>! int32); };
